    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "multi_select": false,
    "stem": "Consider the following custom module that stores hidden layers in a standard Python list. What will `len(list(model.parameters()))` evaluate to?",
    "code": "import torch.nn as nn\n\nclass MLP(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.hidden = [nn.Linear(16, 16), nn.Linear(16, 16)]\n        self.out = nn.Linear(16, 4)\n\n    def forward(self, x):\n        for layer in self.hidden:\n            x = layer(x)\n        return self.out(x)\n\nmodel = MLP()\nprint(len(list(model.parameters())))",
