      "B": "`loss` is a 0D tensor attached to the entire forward computation graph (`grad_fn`); writing `running_loss += loss` keeps references to the computation graph of every batch in the epoch alive in memory, preventing garbage collection and rapidly causing an Out-Of-Memory (OOM) error.",
