    "stem": "What happens if a custom `Dataset.__getitem__(self, idx)` returns a dictionary `{'features': torch.randn(10), 'target': torch.tensor(1)}` and you iterate over `DataLoader(ds, batch_size=32)`?",
    "code": "class DictDataset(Dataset):\n    def __len__(self):\n        return 64\n    def __getitem__(self, idx):\n        return {'features': torch.randn(10), 'target': torch.tensor(idx % 2)}\n\nloader = DataLoader(DictDataset(), batch_size=32)\nbatch = next(iter(loader))",
