    "stem": "A neural network contains `nn.BatchNorm1d(128)` layers and is trained in `model.train()` mode on a dataset of $N = 1,025$ samples with `DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=32, shuffle=True, drop_last=False)`. At the very last step of the first epoch, training crashes with:\n`ValueError: Expected more than 1 value per channel when training, got input size torch.Size([1, 128])`.\nWhat is the cleanest `DataLoader` configuration change to prevent this crash during training?",
