    "multi_select": false,
    "stem": "You are training a time-series forecasting model on hourly electricity demand recorded from January 2023 to December 2025. Why is applying `torch.utils.data.random_split` (or `train_test_split(..., shuffle=True)`) across all hourly timestamps a severe methodological error?",
    "code": "# Hourly time-series records ordered chronologically from 2023 to 2025:\ntrain_ds, test_ds = random_split(timeseries_ds, [0.8, 0.2])",
