      "A": "Because `random_split` only works on 2D image tensors, not 1D time-series tensors.",
      "B": "Because time-series models require the test set to come chronologically *before* the training set.",
      "C": "Because random splitting causes **temporal (look-ahead) data leakage**: the model trains on future timestamps (e.g., 2:00 PM and 4:00 PM on a given day in 2025) and is evaluated on intermediate past timestamps (e.g., 3:00 PM on that same day).",
      "D": "Because `random_split` changes the sampling frequency of the timestamps."
