    "stem": "You have a normalized image tensor `norm_img` of shape `(3, 224, 224)` that was normalized with `transforms.Normalize(mean=[0.485, 0.456, 0.406], std=[0.229, 0.224, 0.225])`. How do you mathematically invert (un-normalize) `norm_img` back to the `[0.0, 1.0]` range for visualization with `plt.imshow`?",
    "code": "mean = torch.tensor([0.485, 0.456, 0.406]).view(3, 1, 1)\nstd = torch.tensor([0.229, 0.224, 0.225]).view(3, 1, 1)\n# Given norm_img = (img - mean) / std, recover img in [0.0, 1.0]:",
