    "stem": "When writing a custom transformation class to pass inside `transforms.Compose([..., AddGaussianNoise(0.0, 0.1)])`, which special method must `AddGaussianNoise` implement (assuming it does not subclass `nn.Module`) so that `transforms.Compose` can invoke it on each sample?",
    "code": "import torch\n\nclass AddGaussianNoise:\n    def __init__(self, mean=0.0, std=0.1):\n        self.mean = mean\n        self.std = std\n\n    # Which method makes instances callable by transforms.Compose?",
