    "stem": "Suppose a dataset has $N = 1,001$ samples and you call `torch.utils.data.random_split(dataset, [0.8, 0.2])` using fractional proportions. How does PyTorch handle fractional lengths when $0.8 \\times 1001 = 800.8$ and $0.2 \\times 1001 = 200.2$?",
    "code": "from torch.utils.data import random_split\n\n# len(dataset) == 1001\ntrain_sub, val_sub = random_split(dataset, [0.8, 0.2])\nprint(len(train_sub), len(val_sub))",
